d episode of game  of thrones now why that's disappointing  to me is because  he puts horror into this revenge flick  which i like it's this epic viking story  right i like that he's putting in his  style still but you'll see certain  critics say oh but it didn't affect you  know him being robert eggers i totally  disagree on that because what makes  robert eggers so great is that his  stories are always incredibly smart and  you're thinking about the film for a  long time after and they all end on a  you know haunting moment that stays with  you it just gives you that feeling and  you know what i'm talking about if  you've seen his previous films that  doesn't happen here this is actually a  movie like most revenge tales you can  shut your brain off and that's  incredibly disappointing for robert  eggers and that's where my  disappointment this film comes is in the  story where it's not this incredibly  smart story like his other two films and  you're not going to be thinking about  this movie afterwards you're just going  to watch it say that was a pretty good  time i'm entertained but it just feels  like a really good blockbuster and  i think that that's good but when we  know who's directing it it's  disappointing so you have to look at it  in different ways where i think so many  people like the film i really enjoyed  the film and i thought it was a really  really good film like i was entertained  the whole time i wasn't bored and like i  said production design is off the chart  score is incredible here acting's great  right you got this a-list cast but  before we get into the acting for a  second i do want to make that point that  still though that is where you can add  all this big stuff in a bigger budget  but again yes what the fear was of what  i originally had that he was going to do  an epic revenge tale that was gonna  maybe box him in from doing his ultimate  high ceiling where he can go places  where your brain didn't think you could  go from film and something that sticks  with you and it just doesn't happen here  and guess what if you're waiting for  that classic robert eggers like you know  shot to end the movie that like makes  you feel like wow like no like this  isn't that movie that people are going  to go on reddit and talk about for days  and you know have something that's  making your brain stimulated it's just  not it and that's disappointing yeah so  that fear that i felt when he signed up  for this there you go like i just don't  think it was the best decision for him  to do it you know maybe business-wise  yes it's the best decision but for the  art yeah no it's just like it seems like  he's just having fun making a really  good epic revenge show and if that's  what you're looking for from him that's  great but for me it's just disappointing  to know what he's actually capable of  and then seeing him kind of doing this  so he's really good at it though you  know and it it's that feeling that  visually everything here feels unique  and different that's where it stands out  but the story beats right you've seen  before the message you've seen before  you know it's the blend of game of  thrones the revenant it's those type of  stories that  in a film you know you know where it's  going from the beginning there's a twist  in it that's okay you know it's the  twist we've seen before and then the  message has been done to death so that's  where i was just shocked how unoriginal  those parts were and that's the problem  a lot of tales it could be in any  timeline when it's a revenge story a lot  of times it it's so hyper focused on  that that it doesn't even give a moment  to breathe for character and a lot of  side characters are very thin and that  happens here too and i think  the acting's amazing right you got this  great cast with alexander scarzard anja  taylor joy willem dafoe who i wish was  in the film more bjork who's in here for  five minutes nicole kidman was pretty  good but i've seen her do 